<title>FRANCE: Paribas confirms SocGen placing.</title>
<headline>Paribas confirms SocGen placing.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Paribas confirmed that it had executed a bought deal on Wednesday after bourse closing, placing 1,221,500 shares in Societe Generale at 570 francs to institutional investers.</p>
<p>The deal, for a block representing 1.33 percent of Societe Generale's share capital, raised 696 million francs.</p>
<p>The block represented a stake held by Navigation Mixte, the holding company in which Paribas took control earlier this year and is busy selling non-strategic assets to turn the group around.</p>
<p>Paribas earlier this year sold Navigation Mixte's stake in Compagnie Francaise de Sucrerie to Eridania Beghin-Say and halved its stake in tobacco group Seita to 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>Paribas said that it was sole lead manager and bookrunner for the Societe Generale deal.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
